isdom to hikers, yet his principles remained solid, as he once even refused the company of three Supreme Court justices. Enter the forest with author and Ownby friend Carroll McMahan as he tells the hilarious, dramatic and fascinating stories of a man who truly lived on his own terms\"--","\"A history of the life of Lem Ownby\"--","Includes bibliographical references (pages 119-122) and index"],"isbn":"9781626191198","language":"eng","lccn":"2013037056","mediatype":"texts","old_pallet":"IA-NS-0001569","openlibrary_edition":"OL27577587M","openlibrary_work":"OL20365278W","operator":"associate-sherwin-pasaylo@archive.org","page-progression":"lr","publisher":"Charleston, SC : The History Press","rcs_key":"24143","repub_state":"19","scanner":"station66.cebu.archive.org","scanningcenter":"cebu","scribe3_search_catalog":"isbn","scribe3_search_id":"9781626191198","subject":["Ownby, Lem, 1889-1984","Mountain life -- Tennessee -- Elkmont Region -- Anecdotes","Mountain life -- Great Smoky Mountains National Park (N.C. and Tenn.) -- Anecdotes","Elkmont (Tenn.) -- Biography","Great Smoky Mountains National Park (N.C. and Tenn.) -- Biography","Great Smoky Mountains National Park (N.C. and Tenn.) -- Anecdotes"],"title":"Elkmont's Uncle Lem Ownby : sage of the Smokies ","tts_version":"5.3-initial-170-ga5e5737d","uploader":"station66.cebu@archive.org","publicdate":"2022-11-29 17:01:53","access-restricted-item":"true","identifier-access":"http://archive.org/details/elkmontsunclelem0000mcma","identifier-ark":"ark:/13960/s2h8mcfd0v9","scandate":"20221129175901","imagecount":"134","autocrop_version":"0.0.14_books-20220331-0.2","ppi":"360","republisher_operator":"associate-shielamae-olmilla@archive.org","republisher_date":"20221201162550","republisher_time":"254","foldoutcount":"0","bookplateleaf":"0002","ocr":"tesseract 5.2.0-1-gc42a","ocr_parameters":"-l eng","ocr_module_version":"0.0.18","ocr_detected_script":"Latin","ocr_detected_script_conf":"0.9020","ocr_detected_lang":"en","ocr_de